{
  "title": "Ledger postings: balance across entries, rows and accounts",
  "proves": ["every journal entry balances: its debits equal its credits (L1)", "a line posts to an account that is open on the posting day (L2); the closing day itself is open", "a line has one positive side (L3) and the currency of its account, for invoice lines and payment lines (L4)", "the balance of an account never goes below zero on its normal side, with the lines in posting order: day, posting_rank (invoices before payments), line id (L5)", "a payment is split over the open invoices of its customer in proportion to the open amounts, to the cent: the largest remainder method puts the extra cent on I1 in AL01 (719) and not on I2 (2281) (L6)", "a payment pays only invoices of its own customer dated on or before its payment day (L6)", "the tax is rounded to the nearest cent, half up, and the gross is net plus tax (L7)", "no line is posted after the period close, and the close day itself is open (L8)", "the trial balance holds: total debits equal total credits", "a payment above the open amount of its customer is reported as infeasible", "the same model, data and seed give the same postings on every run"],
